-- ============================================================================
-- 40: render-replica LIVE (EMITTER body mode) — EFFECTS rendering. The pure
-- Effect-Poly nodes (hitsparks/energy/projectiles/supers/auras, cat 1..4 with GFX2
-- in 0x0CED0000) were ABSENT because the emitter SKIPS isEffect sats (finding 37)
-- and render_frame.wasm (whose walker WOULD draw them) does NOT draw in the live
-- emitter default. This routes each effect node to a baked EFFECTS ATLAS and draws
-- it as an additive own-origin quad, engZ-sorted against the bodies. 2026-06-15.
-- Apply: tools/re_kb/rekb.sh @tools/re_kb/40_replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas.surql
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:emitter_effects_pass_code SET kind='js_function',
  ref='web/webgpu/sprite-client.mjs buildEmitterDrawList (isEffect branch) + _emitEffectQuad + _resolveFxSprite + loadFxAtlas (FX_CID=0xFE0); web/render-replica/replay.html renderBodiesPass (FX_CID setAtlas register) + populateObjectsFromRAM (isEffect/effect_key)',
  note='LIVE replay default __bodyMode=emitter -> renderBodiesPass -> buildEmitterDrawList is what REACHES THE SCREEN (render_frame.wasm computes a validation-only TA, does NOT draw). populateObjectsFromRAM tags each pool node isEffect = (node+0x15C low28 in 0x0CED0000..0x0CEE0000) and carries effect_key = node+0x15C & 0xFFFF + engZ = 1/(node+0xE8). buildEmitterDrawList`s isEffect branch (was: skipSel++ continue, finding 37) now calls _emitEffectQuad: resolve the effects-atlas sprite (this.chars[FX_CID], baked from the disc Effect-Poly bank, sprite-keyed by BOTH dir idx 0..24 AND effect_key=(0x0CED03D8+idx*0x10)&0xFFFF), draw ONE additive quad at the node`s OWN screen pos o.x/o.y (node+0xE0/E4) with the bake`s point-centered own-origin offset (dx=-wG/2,dy=-hG/2), z=engZ*1e6 (engZ-less -> 1e3 = near = on top of bodies). charId=FX_CID so the GPU`s per-cid byChar group binds the fx texture; item.blend=0x01 selects pipeAdd (dst=ONE glow). Gated window._fxEmit (cockpit EFFECTS knob).';

UPSERT source:effect_poly_directory SET kind='oracle_capture',
  ref='_effects_capture/mc_effects.log (Effect-Poly dump, dirBase = *(0x0CED0008) = 0x0CED03D8) + _effects_capture/atlas/fx_atlas.{json,png} (25 dir textures baked from each entry e8 VRAM addr); deployed web/test-atlas/effects/fx_atlas.{json,png} (gitignored, ROM-derived)',
  note='The Effect-Poly directory at 0x0CED03D8 holds 25 valid 0x10-byte entries (idx 0..24): e0=size (128x128 or 256x256), e8=VRAM tex addr (0x0CDA4000..), fmt ARGB4444/RGB565/ARGB1555. STATIC + resident this capture. The fx_atlas bake is DUAL-keyed: sprite["<idx>"] AND sprite["<effect_key>"] where effect_key=(0x0CED03D8+idx*0x10)&0xFFFF (984+idx*16). CRITICAL OPEN: the live binding from an effect node to a directory entry is UNPROVEN offline — mc_effects.log is a directory-only dump (40 frames, zero per-node rows). _resolveFxSprite therefore tries 3 keys in order: (1) effect_key=node+0x15C&0xFFFF (direct, if node+0x15C IS a dir-entry address); (2) dirIdx=(effect_key-0x03D8)>>4 (dir-offset model); (3) raw node+0x144 sid as a dir index. window.__fxBindLog logs the resolved (effect_key,dirIdx,sid->chosen) per node ONCE; window.__fxMiss() lists effect_keys that bound nothing. These make the true binding OBSERVABLE in the live browser so it can be locked from a contact frame.';

UPSERT finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas SET
  statement='BUILT 2026-06-15 (browser-validation pending a live contact frame). The render-replica EMITTER (the live default draw path) now RENDERS pure Effect-Poly effects (hitsparks / energy / projectiles / supers / auras), closing the isEffect half of OPEN finding:replica_emitter_sat_own_gfx2_atlas. ASSESSMENT of what the engine draws (slot-table walk 0x8C2895E0/0x8C287DE0 + node fields): three classes — (A) BODY-bank satellites (projectiles sharing a resident fighter GFX, body-range sels) already render via the owned-pose path (finding 37); (B) PURE Effect-Poly nodes (cat 1..4, GFX2/GFX1 in 0x0CED0000) were ABSENT — skipped by the emitter, and render_frame.wasm (which WOULD walk them, finding:replica_effect_walker_faithful) does not draw in emitter mode; (C) the stray foot-fragments were the finding-37 wrong-Z owner-atlas misdraw (now skipped). FIX for class B: route each isEffect node to the baked EFFECTS ATLAS (fx_atlas, the 25 disc Effect-Poly dir textures), drawn as ONE additive own-origin quad at node+0xE0/E4 (the SAME own-origin rule the whole-sprite buildDrawList`s FX_CID path uses), engZ (1/W from node+0xE8) sorted against the bodies so a foreground spark draws OVER and a back aura BEHIND. Blend = additive (dst=ONE) so energy/sparks glow. The GPU needs no change: FX_CID is registered as a pseudo-char (replay.html renderBodiesPass SG.setAtlas) and flows through the existing byChar/pipeAdd path; no charPal -> the recolor shader is a no-op (effects pass through their pre-colored RGB). KNOWN LIMITATION: the node->directory binding is UNPROVEN offline, so _resolveFxSprite tries effect_key, then dirIdx, then sid, and the unbound set is surfaced via __fxMiss()/__fxBindLog for live locking. The fx textures are point-centered 128/256px bakes (no per-effect anim frame / no cumulative pen) — a coarse but visible approximation of the engine`s walker-emitted multi-cell effect; the faithful path remains the render_frame walker (needs the Effect-Poly GFX shipped on the wire, finding:replica_live_satellite_gfx_residency, OPEN). COCKPIT (browser validation): EFFECTS panel — fx emit on/off (window._fxEmit), fx dx/dy/scale nudge (window._fxCfg), fx binding log (window.__fxBindLog); buttons __fxNodes()/__fxAtlas()/__fxMiss(); plus window._satRenderMode=off isolates pool sats. Deployed cache-bust: replay.html sprite-client import ?v=fxemit1; fx_atlas scp-only to /var/www/maplecast/test-atlas/effects/ (ROM-derived, NEVER committed). Branch feat/render-replica-live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='medium', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->cites->source:emitter_effects_pass_code;
RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->cites->source:effect_poly_directory;
RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->cites->routine:loc_8c030af8;
RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->about->finding:replica_emitter_sat_own_gfx2_atlas;
RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->about->finding:replica_effect_walker_faithful;
RELATE finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas->about->finding:replica_live_satellite_gfx_residency;

-- ---- OPEN: lock the live node->directory binding from a contact frame ----
UPSERT finding:replica_effect_fx_binding_unproven SET
  statement='OPEN (raised 2026-06-15). The effects atlas resolves a live effect node to a baked sprite via 3 fallback keys (effect_key=node+0x15C&0xFFFF, dirIdx=(effect_key-0x03D8)>>4, raw sid) because the TRUE binding was never captured (mc_effects.log dumps only the directory, no per-node rows; prod replica-live captures so far were idle / had only body-bank sats). LOCK IT: on a live prod contact frame (fire a hitspark/projectile/super), open replay.html, set window.__fxBindLog=true, and run __fxNodes() — record, per Effect-Poly node, node+0x15C (effect_key), node+0x144 (sid), node+0xE0/E4, and WHICH atlas sprite (if any) it resolved + whether it looked correct on screen. That row set IS the binding table; bake it into _resolveFxSprite (drop the wrong fallbacks). If NONE of the 3 keys hit (atlas misses, __fxMiss non-empty), the node+0x15C is not a dir-entry address at all (likely the GFX1 pixel base or a TCW) -> capture node+0x15C/+0x160 and the live TCW and re-derive the dir-entry selection (the engine`s loc_8c030af8 -> texture-submit reads the directory via some index we have not pinned). Cross-ref the camera work (mvc2-sh4-re-expert) since effect anchors share the node+0xE0/E4 world->screen transform the camera scales.',
  status='open', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:replica_effect_fx_binding_unproven->about->finding:replica_emitter_effects_fx_atlas;
